## 10. Determine Scope

Search for related activity across:

- Additional endpoints
- Additional accounts
- Additional domain controllers
- Similar PowerShell commands
- Additional scheduled tasks
- Additional privileged-group changes
- Additional remote logons
- Related authentication failures

Questions:

```text
Is the activity isolated to one endpoint?
Was the account used elsewhere?
Were additional persistence mechanisms created?
Were other privileged accounts modified?
```

---

## 11. Validate Authorization

Determine whether the activity corresponds to:

- Approved administrative work
- Change-management activity
- Security testing
- Helpdesk activity
- Software deployment
- Planned maintenance

If authorized:

```text
Validate
   |
   v
Document
   |
   v
Close
```

---

## 12. Escalation Criteria

Escalate when:

- Activity cannot be validated
- Credentials appear compromised
- Multiple systems are affected
- Encoded PowerShell is unexplained
- Persistence is unauthorized
- Privileged membership is unauthorized
- Activity continues after initial detection
- Additional related alerts are observed

---

## 13. Containment Considerations

For a confirmed incident, response may include:

- Disable compromised accounts
- Remove unauthorized privileged membership
- Remove malicious scheduled tasks
- Isolate affected endpoints
- Reset credentials
- Review adjacent systems
- Preserve relevant logs
- Escalate to incident response

Containment actions should follow organizational policy and authorization procedures.

